Title: 
  The Zombie-Film Afterschool
  a "sophomore effort" special
Credit: by
Author: Cameron King

Thursday the 16th, 2017. Spenville, Illinois.

INT. CROSBY HOUSE - DAY

We open on a shifting black, with swells of gray colors in gradients and the occasional texture of something like hair. Throughout all this, the sound of something buzzing comes into focus. Soon, we have panned out just enough to see that the dark, hairy, buzzing thing is in fact a fly. It lands on a mirror and is immediately squashed in a bit of tissue paper.

CUT TO:

A wider view and see the person responsible for the fly's death - it's GILLIAN CROSBY, a high school senior girl with relatively short, brunette hair with bangs which curls a bit at the bottom. She is dressed in a white cardigan and has very thick glasses that make her eyes look slightly larger than they should be. Despite all these things, she carries herself with confidence. She crushes the tissue paper into a ball and tosses it into the trash, and continues applying some makeup and is about to put on chapstick. From offscreen, we hear a muffled voice.

GILLIAN'S MOM
GILLIAN!

GILLIAN
Coming!

She puts down the chapstick and exits the scene, but we linger on it for a few more seconds, hearing the sound of her walking out fading into...

INT. CAR - MOMENTS LATER

A mid-2010s indie synthpop track that is playing on Gillian's headphones (picture some white girl banger) with tinny quality. Her lips are dry and she appears to be chewing at them. She watches out the window as the car moves across town, we see various minor characters going about their morning routine, like a couple holding hands, a boy wearing shorts and a hoodie feeding his dog, and a girl with sunglasses looking at her phone. As the car lurches to a halt because of a red light, she looks to see a tall, dark haired boy talking to someone facing away from Gillian. This is LOUIS.

Gillian blushes at the sight of Louis, who notices her and gives her a soft smile. She smiles and waves to him shyly. He waves back.

Standing next to Louis is DEREK, who has been facing away from Gillian until now. As Louis waves, Derek follows his gaze with a scowl. As he does, something in his face shifts for just a second, before the music stops and there is a

FREEZE FRAME + TITLE CARD, IN LARGE, EXCESSIVELY SERIF-ED RED LETTERS WITH ERRATIC PLACEMENT AND SCALE: 
THE ZOMBIE-FILM AFTERSCHOOL.

INT. CLASSROOM - DAY

Gillian is in class, sitting at her desk, completing a test. As she finishes it and turns the paper over, she looks up to see her teacher, talking to another teacher just outside the classroom. One teacher hands the other a red binder. She disregards this and picks up a book which appears to be the script to "Nocturnal Animals."

The boy next to her takes the opportunity of the teacher looking away to peek at her test in the least subtle way possible. She notices, and he looks ahead, stiffening up. She rolls her eyes and flips her paper back up so her answers are visible, rubbing her fingers together to signal "money, please." The boy nods, quickly copying her answers.  

INT. SCHOOL HALLWAYS - MOMENTS LATER

As the bell rings, Gillian leaves the class while slipping a 10-dollar bill into her wallet. As she is about to make her way down the hallway, she notices Louis and doubles back to put her out of his sight. Coming from behind her is KATIE, Gillian's best friend, who squeals, causing Gillian to jump in fright.

KATIE
Ohmygosh Gillie! It's been, like, so long!

GILLIAN
Jesus, Katie! You spooked me. Nice to see you at school again.

KATIE
Sorry! Here, we can hug now, I don't have whooping cough anymore. I could've called with the news, but I wanted to surprise you.

GILLIAN
Well, jeez. Job well done.

KATIE
Now, you're going to need to get me up to speed on everything that's happened while I was out. First, though...

She peeks down the hallway that Gillian just retreated from.

KATIE (CONT'D)
Is there a new reason why you're running away from Louis with your face all blush-y, or is still the same?

GILLIAN
You know me too well.

KATIE
I know you just enough. You don't like to admit it, Gillie, but you're a hopeless romantic at heart.

GILLIAN
You're going to bring it up, aren't you?

KATIE
(mischievously)
Oh yes, I am. 

She pouts and brushes her hair to imitate Gillian's bangs.

KATIE (CONT'D)
(mocking)
"Won't someone be the Jack to my Gillian?"

Gillian buries her face in her hands.

KATIE (CONT'D)
That's you. That was you in tenth grade. That was an actual thing you said.

GILLIAN
This is going to haunt me all my life.

KATIE
I respect the analogy. Lots of sensual content in the poems of Mother Goose, y'know?

GILLIAN
shutupshutupshutup

KATIE
Just, climbing that big ol' hill... fetching that wet, wet pail of water...

GILLIAN
Okay. In my defense - at that time I was heavily crushing on a particular Jack.

KATIE
Oh my God. Black?

GILLIAN
What? No, white. Nicholson.

Katie's jaw drops.

KATIE
Is that why you made us watch The Shining together?

GILLIAN
I said I was sorry.

KATIE
That movie traumatized me!

GILLIAN
I said I was sorry!

KATIE
How many little sisters do I have?

GILLIAN
(embarrassed)
Two?

KATIE
Correct. And what are they?

GILLIAN
(embarrassed)
Twins.

KATIE
You're an only child, so I can't expect you to be empathetic towards other people, but I hope you have some idea about how embarrassing it is to be scared of your little sisters.

GILLIAN
... did they ever ask you to play with them?

KATIE
Like, every day.

A second passes, then the two of them burst out laughing. Katie's laugh, in particular, bursts into a series of coughs and gasps which sound identical to the sound of whooping cough.

GILLIAN
Are you good?

KATIE
Yeah, probably. Shit, bell's over. We gotta get to the cafeteria.

The two start walking offscreen. Like before, the camera remains where they were standing for a second, listening to the two of them walk off until the sound of a fire drill rings though the school. After a second, a crowd of students shuffle their way down the hallway. Among them are Katie and Gillian. Katie is looking around frantically, covering her ears. Gillian looks exasperated. We follow them as they talk.

GILLIAN
Again, really?

KATIE
Has this been happening a lot?

GILLIAN
Like, three times this week.

KATIE
Seriously? Do they have a quota of fire alarms they have to fill?

GILLIAN
Scheduled fire alarms, yes. These are unscheduled.

The two exit with the crowd into the courtyard.

EXT. COURTYARD - MOMENTS LATER

Dozens of children gather in the grassy area in front of the school, the neat units that they had been forced into by teachers and administrators quickly dissolving as people walked about trying to find their friends. As we move through the crowd we hear the voices of several teens.

TEEN 1
...third time this week, I swear-

TEEN 2
Nah, it's gotta be four.

TEEN 3
...this didn't happen during my test. I would've been...

TEEN 4
...A movie date is nice but how do I....

TEEN 5
....They'll see soon. They'll all see.

TEEN 6
...God DAMN my balls itch. What the fuck...

We linger on Gillian and Katie talking for a few seconds...

KATIE
Look, if you don't talk to him I'm gonna do it for you.

GILLIAN
You keep your mouth shut, okay?

... before moving on.

TEEN 7
...I dunno. She always seemed creepy to me. Didn't you hear...

TEEN 8
... dreamt I was an animal. Just a little baby calf, the noises I was making...

On the outskirts of this crowd, leaning against the wall, is a slouchy, scruffy looking teen with warm, messy blonde hair and a permanent scowl. It's Derek, the boy from earlier. He takes a stray cigarette from his pocket and tries to light it, failing.

LOUIS
(from offscreen)
You don't smoke.

Derek huffs, shoving the cigarette back into his pocket. Louis takes his lighter, examining.

DEREK
Hey! Give that back!

LOUIS
Here, you were fucking it up. You've gotta pull down on the wheel and press the button at the same time.

He demonstrates, setting off the lighter. Derek swipes for it but Louis pulls away.

DEREK
Very cool, Lou. Now, are you gonna give that back to me?

LOUIS
Maybe. I'll trade it for your cigarettes.

DEREK
You can't do that! That belongs to me!

Louis gives him an disbelieving look. Derek blushes, then looks down.

DEREK (CONT'D)
OKAY, it belongs to Gerald. So you REALLY have to give that back.

LOUIS
Cigarettes, please.

Derek grumbles something unintelligible, but hands over the cigarettes. Louis smiles, handing over the lighter, which Derek immediately tries to operate, still failing.

LOUIS (CONT'D)
What'd you say?

DEREK
I said "I can buy more cigarettes."

LOUIS
Yeah, well, you still can't work a lighter, so I'm not that worried about your lungs just yet.

Louis leans back against the wall. Derek, as usual, is scowling. He looks back at the crowd.

DEREK
The girl from before. The one from the car.

LOUIS
Who, Gillian?

DEREK
Yeah, she's staring at me.

CUT TO:

Gillian is, in fact, staring at Louis, squeezing her hand open and shut as if she's deliberating whether to wave or not. Katie is giving her notes.

KATIE
Okay, you're gonna want to, like, flutter your eyelashes a bit. And then you can bite your lip and you gotta - shit, don't wave like that!

GILLIAN
What? Why not? It's a great wave.

KATIE
Yeah, for a Queen Elizabeth impression. We're trying to... wait, what? Louis is over there, right?

GILLIAN
Um, yeah. Is this wave better?

KATIE
No, worse. Don't sway. Why is Louis hanging out with... Derek Sandoval?

GILLIAN
Oh yeah, I saw them hanging out earlier. Is that weird?

KATIE
Uh, yeah! He's a junior. And he's a fucking freak. Total weirdo.

CUT TO:

Louis and Derek are watching the two girls through the rest of the crowd, baffled.

LOUIS
Okay, that's gotta be a fitness thing. Like an exercise or something.

DEREK
You sure she's not waving at me?

LOUIS
In what world is that waving?

DEREK
Wow. First time a girl gives some attention to me instead of you and already you're getting jealous. Bad look, dude.

The crowd of teens begins shuffling back inside and the boys slip in with them.

INT. SCHOOL HALLWAYS - CONTINUOUS

Louis and Derek walk side-by-side. Behind them in the distance, Gillian lamely attempts a frantic wave, which neither notice. Katie swats her, and the two rush ahead of the boys.

DEREK
It should be illegal to do these stupid things during my lunch.

LOUIS
This wasn't one of yours?

DEREK
No, I would... Lou, I would tell you if I was going there.

He pouts a bit, looking quite hurt by Louis' suggestion.

DEREK (CONT'D)
You know that, right?

Louis is silent. Behind them, groups of teens peel off to wait outside various classrooms, still chatting.

DEREK (CONT'D)
Do you... go without me ever?

LOUIS
You know I wouldn't do that, Derek. Don't be dumb. Shit, we can't just talk about this right now.

They walk in silence for a bit. Derek is still clearly upset, slouching a little more than usual. Louis looks ahead. After a while, Derek speaks.

DEREK
Are you gonna sit with me at lunch today?

LOUIS
I... I should probably sit with the kids in debate.

DEREK
... Okay.

The two enter the cafeteria, the crowd of teens behind them having thinned to just a few dozen.

INT. CAFETERIA - CONTINUOUS

Derek walks off without saying a word. Louis keeps walking, but watches as he goes. He walks over to a table with a bunch of students who are already talking about something. Two teens scoot apart from each other to make room for him.

MAX
All I'm saying is, there's no real proof for what you're saying. Look, it's definitely weird. No doubt about that.

GILLIAN
Well, just think about it. Oh, uh, hey, Louis.

The camera pans to reveal that Gillian is on the other side of this table, directly across to Louis. Katie sits next to her, looking slightly out of place and occasionally prodding Gillian, gesturing to her and Louis.

LOUIS
Hey, Gillian. What are you guys talking about?

MAX
Gillian thinks the fire alarms are coverups for some big conspiracy.

GILLIAN
Oh, well, that's a bit of a gross exaggeration of what I was saying.

RITA
No, that's exactly what you said.

LOUIS
I'd like to hear her arguments.

Gillian blushes and sputters a bit.

KATIE
What's the matter, Gillie? Something got you flustered?

Gillian shoots her a death glare, and Katie shrinks back. She takes a deep breath and launches into a monologue.

GILLIAN
So I was thinking about the number of fire alarms we've been having, which is, correct me if I'm wrong, six in two weeks?

RITA
Seven.

GILLIAN
Got it. But these aren't scheduled. The weekly newsletter writes about the dates that fire and lockdown drills are going to be on. Technically the only official fire alarm was the first one, last Tuesday. Then we had one on Thursday and Friday. Then one this Monday, two this Tuesday, none yesterday, and one just a few minutes ago.

LOUIS
Could just be some kids pulling it for a prank.

MAX
Fuckin' freshmen. No offense, Neil.

NEIL
I'm a sophomore.

RITA
Jesus, get some heel lifts.

LOUIS
Guys. Gillian isn't done speaking.

GILLIAN
Oh! Um, thank you... Louis. Um, I thought that it would be some kids pulling a prank. But last period, I saw Ms. Johnson get this red binder from Mr. Carlyle, the admin guy.

BEGIN FLASHBACK:

We see earlier, just after Gillian had finished her test, the two teachers talking outside of her class.

GILLIAN (CONT'D, VO)
I didn't think anything of it at the time, but I noticed that she had it later when she was outside.

FADE TO:

The same teacher from before is still carrying the red binder. She opens it and reads names from an attendance list.

MS. JOHNSON
Lianne... Kara... Oliver... Derek? Derek Sandoval? Has someone seen Derek?

END FLASHBACK.

GILLIAN
It's an evacuation folder. Teachers have to use them for these things. Ms. Johnson probably didn't have one, so Mr. Carlyle stopped by to deliver it to her before the drill. Which means...

RITA
The school knew that this was going to happen.

GILLIAN
But they didn't tell us.

KATIE
Wait. But why would they do that?

GILLIAN
That bit, I'm a little foggy on. Discreet locker searches, maybe?

MAX
Principal Redmond doesn't do discreet. Remember Jesse Skyler? There was a whole crowd when he got busted for vaping.

RITA
Fuckin' freshmen.

GILLIAN
Well, what if they weren't looking for drugs? Maybe they were looking for something that required a bit more secrecy?

MAX
(thoughtfully)
Porn.

KATIE
Who brings porn to school?

NEIL
...It's not a... SUPER weird thing to do.

GILLIAN
I don't think it's that. But it has to be something, right?

LOUIS
I like the theory.

KATIE
Yeah. Gillian's a real Nancy Drew, isn't she? She's always coming up with these things.

GILLIAN
...T-thanks, Louis.

RITA
I mean, it's fun, but in my experience, these things are never as serious as we think.

LOUIS
Well, Gillian, you've got at least one believer.

Katie stares at Gillian and mouths "LET'S FUCKING GO" in perhaps the subtle way possible.

CUT TO:

Derek is eating alone. He has a copy of the school newsletter in his hands, and is flipping through it. One page mentions an fire alarm that was planned for Tuesday, November 7, which we linger on for a second before Derek flips the page to an article about the school's debate team. He is staring at a photo of Gillian smiling.

All of a sudden, the bell rings and he carelessly shoves the newsletter into his bag, getting up and briskly walking to his next class. He speeds past Gillian and Katie, who we follow for a bit.

KATIE
I'm telling you, Gillie. He wants you. Bad. You just have to give him that winning smile and he's yours for life.

GILLIAN
Oh, Katie. Geez. I don't think it's that serious. He's just handsome.

KATIE
Husband material. When you first told me about that cute boy on in your little debate club, that was the word you used. And I'm not always the nicest about your choices in boys, but this time you're right, okay?

GILLIAN
...Okay.

KATIE
Now, do you want to bang this boy on prom night?

GILLIAN
(distressed)
I don't know!

The two leave the cafeteria and walk in the hallways.

KATIE
Let me rephrase. Are there any other boys in this repulsive cesspool of a school that you would prefer, over a good-looking, good-SMELLING boy like Louis?
(beat)
And don't say Max. I'm gunning for him.

GILLIAN
Nope. Just Louis.

KATIE
Perfect. You know you want this boy. Are. You. Willing. To. Do. What. It. Takes. To. Get. Him?

GILLIAN
Yes!

KATIE
Good! Now, you have one more class with him today. You HAVE TO ask him out then.

GILLIAN
Wait, what? Today? I can't do that? How am I supposed to... no way! Does it have to be today?

KATIE
Yes. Did you see that Rita chick? She was eating that apple all sensually up in his face. You need to act fast.

GILLIAN
No way! Rita's nice.
(beat)
How does one sensually eat an apple?

KATIE
She was peeling it, okay? And making eyes. Whatever. You do this right now, or you'll never do it. Look, this is my class. I've got to go.

She walks to the area outside of a class, leaving Gillian in the hallway. As she checks her nails, the same boy who was asking Gillian for test answers comes up to Katie.

BOY
Hey, um. Katie? So, I didn't do the homework, and-

KATIE
What makes you think I did it?

INT. CLASSROOM - DAY

Derek glumly chews on a pencil. We tilt down to reveal that he's filling out an algebra sheet with a similarly chewed pencil. He huffs in frustration at something on his paper, putting down his chewed pencil and fishing a fresh pencil out of his bag, which he begins chewing on. Throughout this entire sequence, the girl sitting next to him regards him with increasing disgust.

He takes a moment to scribble on the margins of his notebook. After a moment, we reveal what he's been making - a relatively crude drawing of Gillian. He frowns at the quality, scribbling over it until it's nothing but a dark scratchy splotch on his page. He turns to Neil, next to him.

DEREK
Psst. Hey, Neil.

NEIL
What? Dude, I'm not giving you my answers.

DEREK
So, you've got a girlfriend who's a senior, right?

Neil smiles.

NEIL
Ah... Young master Derek wants to know about the joys of older girls. Well, let me tell you, they know what to do.

DEREK
Umm... okay. I was just wondering... how do I ask one out?

NEIL
Well, you have to understand that the brain of an older girl simply operates on a different level to that of a young man like ourselves.

DEREK
How so?

NEIL
To put it simply, it's their ovaries. The junior girl, you see, she's still a girl. When she becomes a senior, she's a woman, and as such should be treated accordingly.

DEREK
Woah. So, like... flowers?

Romantic shit?

NEIL
If you like. But it's more important to appeal to a woman's more... maternal instincts. It's best if she doesn't see you as a desperate, younger boyfriend, but rather... a son. This is pretty much the only way older woman are going to engage with us.

DEREK
You have got to be bullshitting.

NEIL
No, sir.

Derek looks ahead, disturbed.

DEREK
Got any porn?

NEIL
Always, why?

DEREK
Can I borrow some?

NEIL
No you may not. This is for my use, and my use alone. Speaking of which...

He raises his hand.

NEIL (CONT'D)
Hey, teach?

TEACHER
Yes, Neil?

NEIL
Can I use the bathroom?

CUT TO:

INT. BATHROOM - DAY

We see an occupied stall, and can hear the sound of a pages on a magazine turning, and heavy breathing. Suddenly, Louis walks in, regarding the stall and the noises with relative nonchalance.

LOUIS
Hello, Neil.

The movement in the stall stops. A muffled "shit" can be heard. Louis grins smugly.

LOUIS (CONT'D)
No, it's alright by me. Carry on.

Louis wets his hands, and fixes his hair slightly. He poses himself in the mirror as if he's practicing looking casual.

He whispers a few lines.

LOUIS (CONT'D)
Hello there. No... Hi? Heya there? Gosh, I didn't see you there. Bleh, all these suck. (deep breath) Hi there. Um, I was wondering we could talk about something? I think we should talk. Maybe it's not appropriate to say this, but...
(he sighs)
Look, I think you're really cute. And I was wondering if we could go out sometime?

NEIL
(breathlessly)
Are you talking to me?

LOUIS
(irritated)
Go back to your porn, Neil.

He works his jaw a bit, steeling himself, then walks out of the bathroom.

INT. SCHOOL HALLWAYS - MOMENTS LATER

As Louis walks in the hallways, Gillian rushes up behind him.

GILLIAN
Hey! Louis! Got a moment?

LOUIS
Oh! Hello, Gillian. I was actually just looking for you.

GILLIAN
Hahaha ohmygosh really? That's... so cool. I have also been looking for you. Because. I have something to tell you.

LOUIS
That's interesting. I also have something to tell you.

GILLIAN
Oh, really? Well why don't you say yours, then I'll say mine.

LOUIS
Well, it's not that important.

You can go first.

GILLIAN
Ohmygosh, no, haha. You should go first. Please.

LOUIS
Oh. Well, I was-

GILLIAN
-Actually no, never mind, I have to say this first. I'm-

She's interrupted by the loud ringing of the period bell, signaling the end of the day. Teens begin gathering down the halls.

GILLIAN (CONT'D)
Wow. That was annoying, huh?

LOUIS
You were saying?

GILLIAN
Oh, yeah. Well, Louis, I was thinking-

LOUIS
-And make this quick, please. I have to get to my locker.

GILLIAN
I'm interested in you! Like, romantically. I would like to be your girlfriend. As in, where you are also dating me. As my boyfriend.

Louis stands there for a second, dumbstruck.

LOUIS
Oh.

Gillian looks behind her, where Katie, disguised in sunglasses and a scarf, gives her thumbs up.

Behind Louis, Derek shuffles into the hallway. We see from his perspective, Louis and Gillian talking, unable to hear what they're saying. Derek gasps, looking hurt, and runs in the other direction.

CUT TO:

Louis and Gillian's conversation. Gillian's jaw has dropped.

LOUIS (CONT'D)
... And for all those reasons, plus like 20 that I can't really tell you right now, we shouldn't be dating.

GILLIAN
(weakly)
Okay.

LOUIS
Believe me, this is probably for the best. In fact, you might want to look into just... trying not to have feelings for me at all.

If that's possible.

He rubs the back of his neck awkwardly.

LOUIS (CONT'D)
I really should go to my locker.

Um, so... see you tomorrow.

GILLIAN
Okay! Um, does this change anything between us?

LOUIS
(sighing)
Only if you let it.

He leaves. Katie comes rushing up, pumping her fists.

KATIE
That's right. You fucking did it. I always believed in you... oh. Shit. Tears?

Gillian sniffles a bit.

GILLIAN
No, no. Just, damn, fucking shit in my eyes. Fuck.

KATIE
Um, if it makes you feel better, I always thought he looked kind of ugly. And gay.

Gillian ducks her head and begins to groan.

CUT TO:

INT. CROSBY HOUSE - MANY HOURS LATER

Gillian is lying face down on her bed, still groaning at the same pitch, as if she has been making this noise, uninterrupted, for several hours. Katie is trying to comfort.

KATIE
I mean, he's just a stupid boy. Emphasis on stupid. You know all those girls in the debate team? I bet he steals their ideas and uses them as his own, the chauvinist.

GILLIAN
(muffled)
AAaaaaaaaaauUUUUuggghhHHHH

KATIE
I bet he's got tons of girlfriends. A whole harem. And he beats them all. Guys like Louis, you know. They just take and take.

GILLIAN
(muffled)
I thought you said he was gay.

KATIE
Well, I'm re-evaluating that now! It's 2017. The closet is gone. We killed it! If he was gay, he'd probably just say it or just join drama or something. Instead, he's the head of a club that's all about arguing. Sounds straight to me.
(beat)
Unless he is gay. In which case, it's his duty as a handsome man to tell girls so that they don't end up falling for this.

GILLIAN
(muffled)
I thought you said he was ugly!

KATIE
Well, I lied, okay! I've been trying so hard to make him seem like a bad guy but the truth is you probably just completely fumbled up your chance with the best guy in the school and OHMYGOSH I'm so sorry I said that but it's so true and I don't know how you fucked up so bad!

Gillian gets up, her face flushed and blotchy from the crying. She blows her nose, and sighs.

GILLIAN
I appreciate you for trying. I'm probably just gonna watch an Amy Adams movie.

KATIE
Watching Arrival and listening to Lorde is not going to make you feel better.

GILLIAN
I don't want to feel better. I want to die. I wanna just... crumple to bits and-

Katie (lightly) slaps her across the face.

KATIE
NO! Gillian, you have experienced something very bad today. But mark my words, you are going to get up and you are going to make something of yourself. And the first thing you have to do is move on from that wonderful boy.

GILLIAN
But... how?

KATIE
Distractions! Find a new hobby! Read a book you haven't read before. I dunno, fucking... go for some walks!

GILLIAN
There's no way that's gonna work.

KATIE
Oh, it works, since the beginning of time, humanity has been inventing little rituals to distract ourselves from our troubles. I mean, just look at-

CUT TO:

INT. COHEN HOUSE - NIGHT

MRS. COHEN
Bless us, oh Lord, for these thy gifts that we’re about to receive from thy bounty through Christ our Lord, Amen...

Louis and his family, including his mother, father, and younger sister MELANIE are sitting down at a table in his house. The table is a stark, polished marble, set upon a gray, geometric rug, surrounded by faux-leather cantilever dining chairs that contribute to the overall oppressive modernity of the room. Every article of furniture is gray - the only color in the room is a set of plastic plants in the center of the table and Melanie's bright red shirt.

LOUIS
Amen.

MR. COHEN^
Amen.

MRS. COHEN
...Melanie?

MELANIE
...Amen.

The family begins to eat their food. Mrs. Cohen watches the family for a second, then speaks.

MRS. COHEN
And how was everyone's day? Louis, you had your thing?

Louis pauses.

LOUIS
Oh, yes. The announcement. It wasn't anything crazy, just talking about the debate team on the, erm...

He gestures vaguely with his hands.

LOUIS (CONT'D)
Big speaker. With Rita.

MRS. COHEN
You think more people are going to join now?

LOUIS
That's the hope. I'm doing another one tomorrow, I think.

Everyone continues eating, except Mrs. Cohen, who has not touched her food. She continues watching the family for another second, then speaks again.

MRS. COHEN
And did you like hearing it, Melanie?

Everyone pauses again. Melanie looks up from her food.

MELANIE
What?

MRS. COHEN
Was it cool hearing your brother over the announcements?

MELANIE
I dunno. I listen to his voice enough already.

MRS. COHEN
Well, did anything else happen today?

LOUIS
There was another fire alarm.

MRS. COHEN
Another? That's four this week, right?

She picks up her fork and begins to eat.

MELANIE
...Louis made a girl cry.

Mrs. Cohen sets her fork down. Louis glares at Melanie.

MRS. COHEN
Louis, you didn't!

LOUIS
I did not! She was not crying.

MELANIE
She was after you left.

MR. COHEN
I am very disappointed in you, son.

MRS. COHEN^
Louis...

LOUIS
She's not telling you the full story. A girl asked me out, today. I rejected her offer politely, and with regard for her feelings.

MELANIE
And then she started crying.

MRS. COHEN
Who was it?

LOUIS
Gillian Crosby.

MRS. COHEN
Oh, Louis, she's so nice, though!

MR. COHEN^
The valedictorian?

MELANIE
He also called her ugly. And fat.

Louis puts his fork down, sets his plate aside, and calmly places his hands on the table.

LOUIS
You've forced my hand. I have no choice to bring up the weed I found in your room last week.

The judgmental glares of the parents redirect themselves to Melanie.

CUT TO:

A little later, as Louis is washing the dishes. His father comes up from behind him, stroking his mustache. He gives Louis a pat on the back.

MR. COHEN
Look, son. I think you did the smart thing.

LOUIS
Thanks, Father. I promise you, I really wasn't trying to hurt her feelings.

Mr. Cohen chuckles, looking around to make sure nobody else is listening, then leans in.

MR. COHEN
(whispering)
Yeah, sure. We can cut the act. Look, I know that girl is the only thing standing between you and that valedictorian title. Rejecting at her at this... neurologically vulnerable time in her life is... well, it's a work of genius.

LOUIS
I'm sorry, neurologically vulnerable?

MR. COHEN
Yeah, you know. Senior girl, ovaries and whatnot. It was a good call. Her grades will be plummeting in no time. That, son, is when you swoop in.

Louis finishes drying his last plate, and sets it down.

LOUIS
I should probably go on a walk.

MR. COHEN
Alright, son. Be back by curfew.

Louis walks off, looking seriously concerned.

INT. CROSBY HOUSE - NIGHT

Gillian and Katie are sitting on the couch, watching a movie (preferably Enchanted, starring Amy Adams). Katie is subtly pulling the bowl of popcorn that has been set between them closer to herself. Gillian appears to be in the process of dozing off when the doorbell rings.

GILLIAN
I'll get it.

She walks over to the door, opening it. We don't see who it is at first, but Gillian smiles.

GILLIAN (CONT'D)
Oh, hey. It's you.

We pan to reveal Rita, who is standing on the porch in a coat.

RITA
Hey, Gillian. I was just walking by and I remembered something you might be interested in. Can I come in?

GILLIAN
Oh, of course! Just, um... leave your shoes there.

Rita hangs up her coat, takes off her shoes, and enters the living room.

RITA
Hey, Katie.

KATIE
Hey.

Rita gestures for Gillian to follow her to a more secluded area. Gillian follows.

RITA
Okay, so, you remember how two or so periods before the fire drill, me and Louis went on the announcements to talk about the debate team?

GILLIAN
Yeah?

RITA
Well, all the announcements happen at this speaker area in the office. And while I was waiting in the area for when we were going to speak, I actually overheard some teachers talking about that locker thing you mentioned.

GILLIAN
Discreet locker searches.

RITA
Yeah, that's the one. Didn't seem too important at the time, so I ignored it, but after lunch, I was thinking about your whole story with Mr. Carlyle, and I realized that he was one of the teachers. He was tasked to make sure Ms. Johnson had her emergency binder, just like you said.

GILLIAN
So they were doing locker searches? Did you overhear anything else?

RITA
I was only half-paying attention, sorry. I'm pretty sure they mentioned something about a threat. Like, they were doing the locker search because of some kind of threat.

She checks her watch.

RITA (CONT'D)
Look, it was nice talking to you, but I should probably get going.

GILLIAN
O-okay! Have a safe trip home!

Rita rushes out of the house, giving Gillian a thumbs up as she goes. Gillian sits back down on the couch, looking pale.

KATIE
What was that about?

INT. SANDOVAL HOUSE - NIGHT

Derek lies back in his bed, atop an itchy-looking wool blanket. His room is homely but cluttered, a fine layer of dust covering all of the furniture. He stares up at the incomplete algebra sheet from earlier. It appears as if he's made very little progress on it. He frowns, eyebrows knotted, and his fingers tense, as if he's just barely stopping himself from crumpling the paper into a little ball.

LOUIS
Hope I'm not interrupting anything important.

Derek practically jumps back with a start.

DEREK
Jesus, Lou. You scared me. How'd you get in here?

LOUIS
Your mom likes me. Hey, is that algebra? You've got Mr. Kelly, right?

Louis sits down on Derek's bed, peeking at his paper.

DEREK
Yeah. You had him last year?

LOUIS
Yeah. Well, sophomore year, technically. Let's see... yeah, these assignments always gave me a hard time.

DEREK
Really?

Louis gives him a thin smile.

LOUIS
No, you idiot. I had a 100 in that class.

DEREK
Oh. Well, you wanna do my homework for me?

LOUIS
No can do.

Derek pouts and lightly shoves Louis.

LOUIS (CONT'D)
Sorry, man. I can send you my notes from back then, but that's it.

DEREK
(grumbling)
What's the point of having smart friends if they only help you in the stupidest ways?

Louis just smirks, relaxing. He scans the room.

LOUIS
Hey, where are your ant farms?

DEREK
Oh, they're in that cupboard. Gerald doesn't like it when I have them out.

Louis gets up to the cupboard and opens it.

LOUIS
(irritated)
I ought to punch that bastard in the face sometime.

Derek giggles.

DEREK
I'd love to see you try to throw a punch. He'd deck you.

Louis frowns, but presses onward with his search of the cupboard. Amidst a mess of action figurines and comic books, are a few terrariums. He pulls the first out and sets it on a nearby desk. It's the classic kid's ant-farm complete with plastic scenery and a few sparse tunnels made up from the sand. The second one he pulls out is more sleek and modern-looking, structured by translucent blue gel and fitted with an LED base which gives it a slight glow. He looks in the cupboard and pulls out a third one, a boxy structure which appears more expansive than the others.

LOUIS
Whew, that one's heavy. There any ants in there yet?

DEREK
No. I'm gonna put the ants from the Milton and the gel farm into there soon. Give them some more space.

LOUIS
Ethical concerns, huh? The gel farm doesn't seem so bad.

Derek walks over to the farms.

DEREK
Well, I read on Wikipedia that the gel isn't healthy for them to eat. It's just sugar and preservatives or whatever. Poisons them.

LOUIS
Wikipedia? I wouldn't trust it.

DEREK
I know, I'm just... concerned.

Louis stares at Derek, his playful expression softening for a moment. He opens his mouth like he's about to speak, but he is interrupted.

DEREK (CONT'D)
Are we going to go back there soon?

Louis sighs.

LOUIS
I mean, I'd like to. You have the things?

DEREK
(nodding)
Of course. I mean, I've been trying to go for weeks!

LOUIS
Alright. We could go during the next fire drill. Should be one tomorrow, if we're to believe Gillian's theories.

Derek's face hardens, as if he's just remembering what he saw earlier, remembering that he's decided to be mad at Louis.

DEREK
...Gillian.

LOUIS
Yeah, you remember her. The waving girl.

DEREK
Yeah. You were, um... getting pretty comfy with her after the bell, I saw.

LOUIS
Jesus, you saw that, too?

Derek huffs a bit, looking away.

DEREK
I'm not mad. I guess you were right. She's not interested in me.

LOUIS
Derek, she wasn't asking me out, okay? I was talking to her about some debate club stuff.

DEREK
...Really?

LOUIS
You actually like her?

DEREK
Dunno. She's kinda cute.

LOUIS
Well, I wouldn't go for her, personally. I mean, she doesn't know you. And she's a senior, which is a whole different thing.

DEREK
Yeah, know. She's got ovaries or whatever.

LOUIS
Apparently.

The two sit in silence for a second. Louis looks at the floor for a bit before meekly adding-

LOUIS (CONT'D)
Plus, she already has a boyfriend.

Derek sighs, resting his head in his hands.

DEREK
Of course she does.

The two sit in silence for a bit longer. Louis puts his hand on Derek's shoulder.

LOUIS
Look, um... I don't have anything important going on in my third and fourth periods tomorrow. We can skip then and head back there. Usual meeting spot.

Derek is silent, still glumly looking ahead. Louis shakes him slightly.

LOUIS (CONT'D)
Hey, tell me about your ants. Got any experiments coming up?

Derek sighs.

DEREK
Well, I read on the internet about this pheromone that ants release when they're dead. And how you can buy it in bottle form.

LOUIS
Uh-huh.

DEREK
And I read that if you put a little drop of that on an ant, even if it's still alive, all of the other ants will think it's dead even if it's just walking around, and they'll put it in their graveyard area.

LOUIS
They have graveyards?

Derek grins, unable to contain the excitement building in him.

DEREK
Yup. They're real smart. The gel farm has one right... here, see?

He indicates a small area where some non-moving ants are lying in a pocket within the gel.

DEREK (CONT'D)
It's called, um... necrophoresis, I think. Something along the lines of it. There are these ants which are specifically designed to go and perform the task of dragging the dead body to the graveyard. But they can only tell these things by scent, so if you put something that smells like dead ant in front of them, they're gonna treat it like a dead ant.

Derek turns to Louis, who is watching him intently.

DEREK (CONT'D)
I dunno. Maybe you think it's weird, but I think it's real interesting. I mean, just think about being an ant. You're running around this area filled with thousands of other ants, just surrounded by chemicals and smells that control your thoughts and your job and everything. Can't imagine it.

CUT TO:

INT. SCHOOL - DAY

The students arrive on the high school campus a little after dawn breaks, segmenting off into swarms which taper off to their individual buildings to clog the hallways. They push past each other, rushing to their designated areas, as the sounds of individual voice fade into a babbling cacophony of pubescent, warbling noise...

EXT. SCHOOL COURTYARD - DAY

There is a small field behind the school, the glamorously manicured lawns of the courtyards tapering off into something wild, tall, and overgrown. They droop in the late autumn breeze. We push through the field into a dark, forested area, where leans against a tree, looking around nervously. He makes eye contact with someone we don't see and calms down. Louis walks onscreen.

LOUIS
...Hey there.

DEREK
(nervous)
Hey.

Louis takes a thermos from his bag and offers it to Derek. Derek opens it and frowns.

LOUIS
Might help with the nerves.

DEREK
I'm not drinking beer.

LOUIS
It's gin, actually, straight from my father's basement. Bit of water, too.

DEREK
Yeah, um... I'm good.

LOUIS
More for me, then.

Louis takes a small sip of gin.

DEREK
...Have you been drinking that all day?

LOUIS
Just a bit. Don't want to go in there sober.

The two begin to walk deeper into the woods. Derek pulls a small satchel from his backpack. Louis is looking up at the trees.

EXT. WOODS - CONTINUOUS

LOUIS (CONT'D)
You know where to go?

DEREK
Yeah. When you're close enough, you can kinda smell it.

Louis reaches for his neck, pressing on his collarbone. We can see the indent of a cross necklace hidden beneath his shirt.

LOUIS
Brimstone.

DEREK
What's that?

He sniffs the air, turning to the left. Louis follows.

LOUIS
Sulfur.

DEREK
Oh.
(beat)
Did you know that in Ancient Greece, they used sulfur for fumigation?

They come across an uphill area. Derek begins to pick up large rocks and set check beneath them.

LOUIS
No, I didn't. Hey, isn't it that one, over there?

He points to a rock a bit to the left of Derek. Derek walks over to the rock, and with a bit of effort, picks it up. Beneath it is a small hole, just barely wide enough to fit a person. Louis walks past Derek and puts a crawls in headfirst. Derek watches as the hole swallows Louis. Louis's hand shoots out of the hole, outstretched.

LOUIS (CONT'D)
Light, please.

Derek searches in his bag, and pulls out a small electric lamp, which he passes to Louis. After a second, the hand comes out again. Derek takes it, and is pulled into the cave.

CUT TO:

INT. SCHOOL HALLWAYS - DAY

Gillian is checking her locker, when all of a sudden Rita runs up to her.

RITA
Hey, I can't find Louis. Have you seen him?

GILLIAN
No, I haven't seen him in a bit. What class does he have right now?

RITA
Shit, I don't think there's time. Are you a good speaker?

GILLIAN
No time for what? And why am I-

RITA
Who am I kidding, you're on the debate team! You're a great speaker. Come with me.

She runs off in the direction of the office, and Gillian hesitantly follows, returning to close her locker and then rushing after Rita.

GILLIAN
Where are we going?

RITA
Office. You're going to do the pitch for the debate team with me.

GILLIAN
What?

INT. THE SMALL HELL - DAY

The interior of the cave, when illuminated by the lamp, is a dark, solid red, as if infused with clay or iron. The walls are lined with sheetlike shelves of flowstone that has bends and wobbles that seem almost geologically impossible. The cave is small, and in the center, on a patch of earth, sits Derek and Louis. Derek is retrieving some objects from the bag - a bag of tarot cards, a small radio, a set of rocks. Louis cleans his glasses and takes a swig from his thermos.

DEREK
You see it yet?

LOUIS
No. It's gonna take a bit.

DEREK
I think I can feel it.

Derek's breathing begins to slow and deepen. He removes his shoes, lies back and stares at his feet as he tenses and relaxes in a rhythm. Louis picks up the radio and begins fiddling with it. Voices fade in and out of the static as the volume of it grows.

INT. OFFICE - DAY

A student stands in front of the announcement microphone in the office, reading from a script. This is one of the voices heard in the static.

STUDENT
And the musical selected by the drama club is The Phantom Of The Opera. Get your masks ready!

We push past this student, his voice fading out as we see Gillian sitting on a chair in the waiting room area. She is clearly stressing out about something, reading the script in front of her. Rita sits next to her.

RITA
It's fine, dude. We're gonna have the script with us when we speak. It's not like you're rehearsing.

GILLIAN
This isn't like debate at all. This is like, school-wide, public speaking. I can't handle this. Why didn't you get Max?

RITA
Well, I saw you first.
(beat)
Plus, I thought it might be nice to give you something to do. After what happened.

Gillian sighs, setting her paper down.

GILLIAN
So everyone knows about that whole debacle.

RITA
I'm surprised you had the guts. I mean, you kinda froze whenever he looked at you, huh?

GILLIAN
Don't remind me. I'm moving on, doctor's orders.

RITA
Hell yeah, girl. Look, I've seen this happening to plenty of girls before. Shit, I was crushing on him at one point. Then, I... well, y'know, "figured it out." I kinda had to move on.

GILLIAN
...Figure what out?

RITA
Shit, that's our cue. Get ready.

The two walk up to the microphone.

STUDENT
And now, here to briefly speak about the debate team, we have Rita Smith and Gillian Crosby.

RITA
(reading from script)
Ahem. Do you like constructive discussions? Tournaments? Getting club credits? Well, the Spenville High debate team is looking for members.

GILLIAN
(slowly)
There is... there are... many seats available. Our club is all about learning to improve your skills of conversational analysis and public speaking. We have an upcoming tournament against Argo Community High, so join fast to get a chance to participate.

As she finishes speaking, she shrinks back from the microphone.

RITA
For more information, come to Mr. Pendenski's room at 3pm today.

She steps away from the microphone, turning to Gillian, who is picking up her bag.

GILLIAN
Sorry, I have to get to class quick. Ms. Johnson is kinda strict about these things.

RITA
Oh, alright. See you later?

Gillian rushes off.

INT. THE SMALL HELL - DAY

Louis continues to fiddle with the radio, flicking past static to static, until eventually hearing the drones of some music. He flicks back to a song, lightly distorted in the fuzz. As he sets it down, the song clears up (Pilots by Goldfrapp). He stands up, takes another small swig of his gin, coughing a bit. He sways to the music, pinwheeling his hands slowly.

Derek's breath is becoming interspersed with shudders, cutting up the rhythms with breathy haste.

DEREK
I can feel it.

He sits up, clutching his diaphragm, wheezing slightly. After a few seconds, he calms himself.

DEREK (CONT'D)
Yes, it's here. Can you see it?

LOUIS
Corner of my eye, yes.

Derek begins to rock back and forth slightly, fingers digging into the earth beneath him.

DEREK
What is it?

Louis whips his head around, looking at a patch of the wall.

LOUIS
Hallway. I think it's school.

He reaches out as if to touch something, although there's nothing but rock. Derek watches, still rocking back and forth, the shuddering returning.

LOUIS (CONT'D)
Flip a card.

Derek obliges, flipping over a tarot card from the top of the deck.

DEREK
Five of Cups.

LOUIS
Five of Cups... loss. Grief. Regret, maybe?

DEREK
Your turn. Change the station.

LOUIS
Not yet. I like this song.

DEREK
That's not how this works.

Louis ignores him, continuing to sway.

DEREK (CONT'D)
(whining)
That's not how this-

He catches himself. His hands, caked in dust, rest on his thighs, as he begins to rub that area back and forth, his hands sliding up beyond his hips back to his diaphragm.

DEREK (CONT'D)
Something else is here.

LOUIS
Yes, I can see it. It's... god, it's...

He doubles over, falling to his hands and knees, and begins to vomit.

INT. CLASSROOM - DAY

Gillian reads in class, (the script to American Hustle, starring Christian Bale and Amy Adams) while her classmates complete their work. She looks up to see Ms. Johnson eyeing the emergency binder and sighs.

GILLIAN
Of course.

INT. THE SMALL HELL - DAY

Louis continues to vomit, just barely stopping himself with a sickening gulp. He continues on his hands and knees, looking ill for a second before breathing deeply and looking around.

DEREK
What is it this time?

LOUIS
Horse. Yes, a... white horse. Wild white horse.

He crawls over to Derek, eyes glassy and dazed, and begins to suck the inner area of Derek's bicep. 

DEREK
(spaced out)
I can... oh... off me, you vampire.

Louis pulls off, looking into Derek's eyes. He looks different to how we've seen him before - tired, face discolored, as if some sort of disguise of his has melted away. Derek's face shifts from fear to concern, but as Louis leans in, he still shoves him away.

DEREK (CONT'D)
Get off of me, Lou. Change the station.

Louis stays where he is for a second, just looking at Derek.

DEREK (CONT'D)
That's your job, okay. And I... I can't do this when you're watching.

Louis looks down at the dirt, but does not move.

DEREK (CONT'D)
You smell like puke, okay? Go away.
(beat)
...I'm gonna count to three. One, two-

Louis pushes himself up, walking to the other side of the room and facing the wall.

LOUIS
The white horse.

Derek resumes sliding his hands up and down his thighs and chest.

DEREK
What is it? Like, what is it, really?

LOUIS
... Don't want to know. Check the card.

Derek flips over another card.

DEREK
The tower. I don't know that one.

Louis crouches down again, beginning to dry heave. He pauses for a second to turn to Derek.

LOUIS
Are you done?

DEREK
No. Don't rush me.

Louis vomits again, but this time, the general texture of it quickly fades off into a translucent liquid. He then spits a few more mouthfuls of the liquid.

DEREK (CONT'D)
What is that?

LOUIS
Gin. It's making me throw up the gin. ...I think it wants me sober?

He buries his face in his hands.

LOUIS (CONT'D)
It wants me sober. So I can see it.

INT. SCHOOL HALLWAYS - DAY

Gillian and Katie walk to the cafeteria through the hallways as other students begin to flood the hallway.

KATIE
You're actually doing pretty good. I didn't expect you to be all... fine today. Especially considering yesterday's tears.

GILLIAN
Yeah, well, it's um... probably for the best that I move on quickly. That's what Louis told me.

KATIE
Ugh, what a jerk.

GILLIAN
What? That's jerky?

KATIE
Uh, yeah. That's an objectively jerky thing to say.

The two bump into Rita, who is walking the other direction to her locker.

GILLIAN
Oh, hey, Rita. 

RITA
Hey, Gillian. I just wanted to say that you did great during the announcements.

GILLIAN
...Thanks. You were awesome, too.

RITA
Alright. I just have to get something from my locker, then I'll see you in the cafeteria. 

GILLIAN
Okay. Have fun! I mean, y'know. Get your thing.

She waves awkwardly, then signals to Katie to get her going. Katie drags her along.

KATIE
See you later, Rita.
(beat)
Wow, Gillie. That was bad.

Gillian sighs.

KATIE (CONT'D)
I don't get how you're like, this debate goddess, but unless you're arguing some point you can't hold a conversation to save your life.

GILLIAN
Debating is different from just talking. It's easier. It has a purpose. 

Katie gives her a strange look. All of sudden, the fire alarm bell rings. Gillian and Katie sigh, then turn around.

GILLIAN (CONT'D)
Called it.

KATIE
I knew you were right. I just didn't want to believe you. During our lunch period again?

The two begin to walk back in the other direction. As they keep walking, we can see Rita in the background reach her locker and open it after a brief struggle. The two are closer now. Rita looks in her locker, gasps, and stumbles back. She points at it and is about to say something when-

A massive explosion rips through the hallway, the ball of fire exploding out the locker with enough pressure to knock the two girls back. The students around them immediately rush down the hallways, the usual cacophony of noise going silent for just a second before the screams begin.

INT. THE SMALL HELL - DAY

Derek is stressing, squirming slightly as he continues touching himself, his eyes screwed shut.

DEREK
Change the station.

LOUIS
It wants me to see.

Louis takes off his glasses and drops them behind him, sitting down.

DEREK
(strained)
Change the station, you bastard!

LOUIS
Can't. I can't...

He buries his face in his hands once more.

DEREK
FINE! I'll do it myself!

Derek attempts to sound angry as he grabs the radio, but the effect is diminished by his voice, which seems to indicate that he is seconds away from bursting into tears. He flicks away from the music to static.

INT. SCHOOL HALLWAYS - DAY

The static persists into the next scene, joined by the sound of ringing and muffled screaming as if we can hear out of Gillian's tinnitus-affected ears. Bits of shrapnel have flown into the crowd, and few students stumble or simply fall to the floor in pain - small chunks of metal sticking from their extremities.

Katie grabs Gillian by the arm and attempts to keep her close as the stampede takes over, but Gillian loses her grip and, now not moving as quickly, is pushed forward by the crowd, knocked to the ground by a particularly large and fast student. Katie turns back, but follows the stream, unable to push back.

Gillian is struck by the shoes of her peers again, some carelessly stepping on to her, others narrowly avoiding her, a few even tripping over her prone body, only to push themselves up and continue to stumble onward, fueled by adrenaline. Gillian get up and sidles against a wall to catch her breath out of the way, and as she does so, she can see beyond the mass of trampling legs, an orange glow like fire licking against the walls. The sound of sizzling flesh fades in with the rest of the noise. 

INT. THE SMALL HELL - DAY

Derek is crying, beginning to pick up the materials and put them back into the bag.

A figure which we can't fully see clearly reaches out from behind Louis' shoulder and drops the glasses in his lap. Louis feels this, taking his hands away from his eyes, and his face goes pale with fear. He breathes into the glasses, fogging them up, rubs at them with dirt, but when he looks at them again, they are clear. He snaps them in two, but it simply falls back into his lap fixed. He holds them up to his eyes once more.

Derek drop the deck of tarot cards into the earth. As he scrambles to pick them up, we can see that every face-up card is The Tower.

LOUIS
You want me to see.

A closeup on his eyes cuts to-

INT. SCHOOL HALLWAYS - DAY

Gillian's eyes as the orange glow can be reflected. Most students have run away by now, only a few injured stragglers getting up and hobbling away. A voice rings out on the loudspeakers.

PRINCIPAL ROSS
Students in Building C, please evacuate in a swift and orderly fashion. I repreat, students in Building C, please evacuate in a swift and orderly fashion.

Gillian walks around the corner where the orange glow is coming from, and it seems like the glow is walking towards her as well. As she rounds the corner and sees it, she gasps. The bomb has set the hallway alight - blistering heat and choking smoke flood the hallways. And in the center of it all, someone is on fire.

The pain has reduced this person to little more than an instinctual animal driven to mindlessly amble, bumping into lockers and rushing down dead ends in a fruitless attempt to escape or somehow alleviate the pain. A rattling emerges from the person's throat, as if they have been trying to scream, but like the rest of their flesh, their throat has sloughed off in chunks of charred meat, fading to foul ash on the floor around them.

The person looks at Gillian. And Gillian looks back. As their eyes meet, we see Gillian's face fall. She knows who this is, and so do we.

It's Rita.

Rita reaches out, letting out one final screech of pure agony, as she crumples to the floor, flames tearing through the last of her blackened skin. Gillian begins to hyperventilate, finally running towards the exit. The sounds build again - the screaming, the static, the sizzling, and faintly, the sound of hooves approaching.

INT. THE SMALL HELL - DAY

Derek gathers up the last of the supplies, rushing over to Louis, who is still staring at the wall.

DEREK
Come on. We have to go.

Louis looks at the glasses. The light reflecting off of the glass wavers slightly, as if a figure has walked by.

LOUIS
I can't. I can't.

Derek pulls at him.

DEREK
Lou, please. Louis. I can't leave you here.

Louis works his jaw. In a single quick motion, he slams his glasses against the wall, the fractured glass and metal digging into his hand and cutting it up.

EXT. SCHOOL COURTYARD - DAY

Gillian exits the building, slamming the doors behind her. A crowd of chattering students watch as the fire brigade pulls up. A teacher attempt to bring her towards the crowd, but Gillian shrugs her off, wading out into the grass and sitting down. All sounds fade except the sounds of her breathing, and the nature around her. She looks at her hands. She looks back at the school. From the exterior, it looks completely normal - no real signs of carnage inside. She looks around.

GILLIAN
Katie? Katie, are you there?

She looks out into the woods behind the school. In the distance, she can see two figures approach.

>end of episode one.<





Thanks for reading! :)

-Cameron King




